(3025646, 426742, 25355, '<td valign="top">Wow, this has a great effect on my computer (laptop) screen. The sky can look purple or blue depending on the angle, yet the rest stays essentially the same.</td>', 'Wow, this has a great effect on my computer (laptop) screen. The sky can look purple or blue depending on the angle, yet the rest stays essentially the same.', '2006-11-13 06:17:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3025650, 426503, 25355, '<td valign="top">That''s the Canadian cathedral, if I recall correctly. Good job with the processing.</td>', 'That''s the Canadian cathedral, if I recall correctly. Good job with the processing.', '2006-11-13 06:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(3025652, 426272, 67258, '<td valign="top">I find myself in two minds about this one: On a photographic level my brain just can''t adjust to it - it is too far removed from how I interpret what my eyes see in reality.  That said, I actually rather like it in a sort of jigsaw puzzle painting way - sounds rather as though I am damning it with feint praise, but I am scoring 8, because I do find it curiously attractive, because it is a well composed appealing scene, and because you have avoided the pitfall of horrible skies and halos around the subjects.</td>', 'I find myself in two minds about this one: On a photographic level my brain just can''t adjust to it - it is too far removed from how I interpret what my eyes see in reality.  That said, I actually rather like it in a sort of jigsaw puzzle painting way - sounds rather as though I am damning it with feint praise, but I am scoring 8, because I do find it curiously attractive, because it is a well composed appealing scene, and because you have avoided the pitfall of horrible skies and halos around the subjects.', '2006-11-13 06:21:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3025703, 426521, 67258, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid this doesn''t really hit the mark with me.  Unless I have misunderstod the concept (which is always possible) one of the main advantages of HDR is that it balances out exposure, allowing for areas that would normally be to dark, to be correctly exposed, and yet this photo seems to have large areas that are under-exposed.  Coupled with that, the subject matter and composition are dull and rather uninteresting - a difficult one, though, given the short period in which to take and process the photo!</td>', 'I''m afraid this doesn''t really hit the mark with me.  Unless I have misunderstod the concept (which is always possible) one of the main advantages of HDR is that it balances out exposure, allowing for areas that would normally be to dark, to be correctly exposed, and yet this photo seems to have large areas that are under-exposed.  Coupled with that, the subject matter and composition are dull and rather uninteresting - a difficult one, though, given the short period in which to take and process the photo!', '2006-11-13 06:55:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3025717, 426420, 67258, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous bright, vibrant colours, although on the down-side the greens are rather unnaturally over-saturated.</td>', 'Gorgeous bright, vibrant colours, although on the down-side the greens are rather unnaturally over-saturated.', '2006-11-13 07:00:33.000000', NULL, 1),
