(3047100, 426503, 22748, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top 5 placing! Between you and me, I like this one twice as much as the blue-ribbon winning cathedral shot. This one is so much more vibrant and 3D. (Not to say that the 1st-place shot isn''t good, I liked it too, I just think this one has more powerful lines, and massively greater vibrance.)</td>', 'Congrats on the top 5 placing! Between you and me, I like this one twice as much as the blue-ribbon winning cathedral shot. This one is so much more vibrant and 3D. (Not to say that the 1st-place shot isn''t good, I liked it too, I just think this one has more powerful lines, and massively greater vibrance.)', '2006-11-20 10:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047183, 426546, 326, '<td valign="top">underrated...</td>', 'underrated...', '2006-11-20 10:41:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047194, 426766, 24454, '<td valign="top">Jimmy, CONGRATULATIONS!  This was an amazing challenge with so many standouts!  Top 20 is quite an accomplishment!   The photo is great!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Jimmy, CONGRATULATIONS!  This was an amazing challenge with so many standouts!  Top 20 is quite an accomplishment!   The photo is great! ', '2006-11-20 10:43:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047205, 426521, 15799, '<td valign="top">The sky was totally overcast, the scene dark, the sky wasn''t blown in the photo. HDR was used properly, with 6 exposures over a wide range, and the HDR processing done to faithfully recreate the lighting as I saw it with my eyes, with the exception of a bit of oversaturation to bring up some of the contrasting colors.<br/> <br/>The subject matter was an attempt to portray the expansiveness of the development, the size of the hole in the side of the hill. Unfortunately, that didn''t translate well to the small format. Bad choice on my part.<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the positively presented criticisms.</td>', 'The sky was totally overcast, the scene dark, the sky wasn''t blown in the photo. HDR was used properly, with 6 exposures over a wide range, and the HDR processing done to faithfully recreate the lighting as I saw it with my eyes, with the exception of a bit of oversaturation to bring up some of the contrasting colors. The subject matter was an attempt to portray the expansiveness of the development, the size of the hole in the side of the hill. Unfortunately, that didn''t translate well to the small format. Bad choice on my part. Thanks for all the positively presented criticisms.', '2006-11-20 10:46:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047211, 426376, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow!  The perfect study in HDR!  And thank you so much for sharing exactly how you did it!  I''m so inspired to practice this technique and see if I could ever in a million years achieve photos with this depth of colors and light!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow!  The perfect study in HDR!  And thank you so much for sharing exactly how you did it!  I''m so inspired to practice this technique and see if I could ever in a million years achieve photos with this depth of colors and light! ', '2006-11-20 10:48:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047214, 426824, 24454, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!   I''m not the least bit surprised -- but happy nonetheless that this photo of one of my favorite scenes did so well!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Congratulations!   I''m not the least bit surprised -- but happy nonetheless that this photo of one of my favorite scenes did so well! ', '2006-11-20 10:49:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047221, 426246, 24454, '<td valign="top">The minute I saw this photo, after I picked my jaw up off the floor and studied it for the longest time, I knew it was blue ribbon material!   Congratulations!  This is just flawless!!!!!!<br/> <br/>55 10''s!   WOW!   What a tribute!</td>', 'The minute I saw this photo, after I picked my jaw up off the floor and studied it for the longest time, I knew it was blue ribbon material!   Congratulations!  This is just flawless!!!!!! 55 10''s!   WOW!   What a tribute!', '2006-11-20 10:51:41.000000', NULL, 0),
